# THIS FILE EXISTS TO STOP gcloud FALLING BACK TO .gitignore.
#
# `gcloud builds submit` uploads the build context, and when there is no
# .gcloudignore it generates one FROM .gitignore. That is the wrong rule here:
# .gitignore excludes `data/` and `web/dist/` because they are derived and must
# not be committed — but those are precisely the two directories the container
# image bakes in. Without this file the upload silently omits them and the
# build fails at `COPY data/derived/h3_tables`, several minutes in, with an
# error that points at the Dockerfile rather than at the upload.
#
# Keep this in step with .dockerignore. They answer different questions —
# what is uploaded, versus what the daemon may read — but the same intent.

.git/
.gitignore

# 429 MB of immutable source snapshots. The image carries data/derived only.
data/raw/

# Reinstalled by npm, never read by the runtime image.
web/node_modules/
node_modules/
.venv/
__pycache__/
*.pyc

# The frozen study: provenance for the rules, not an input to the binary.
research/

# Local state.
.dev-logs/
.dev-certs/
.claude/
docs/

# Host-built binaries — wrong architecture as often as not.
api/thirdeye-api
api/api

# The pipeline builds the tables; the image only serves them.
pipeline/

# NOT excluded, deliberately, despite being in .gitignore:
#   data/derived/h3_tables   the parquet the API loads at startup
#   web/dist                 the built SPA the API serves
